<title>UK: Transco UK gas forecasts for April 30.</title>
<headline>Transco UK gas forecasts for April 30.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transco, the transport and pipeline arm of BG plc has announced the following forecasts and data for UK gas consumption in the period 28 to 30 April.</p>
<p>DEMAND:</p>
<p>(mcm = million cubic metres)</p>
<p>Apr 28 (actual) 197 mcm, 46 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Apr 29 (forecast) 206 mcm, 48 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Apr 30 (forecast) 196 mcm, 46 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>TEMPERATURE:</p>
<p>(SNT = seasonal normal temperature)</p>
<p>Apr 28 (actual) 12.4 Celsius, SNT 11.0 Celsius</p>
<p>Apr 29 (forecast) 11.2 Celsius, SNT 11.1 Celsius</p>
<p>Apr 30 (forecast) 12.9 Celsius, SNT 11.2 Celsius</p>
<p>There was no supply interruption called for Tuesday and none expected on Wednesday.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
